WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.760
Add up odd numbers.

2
00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:02.670
One.

3
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.590
One plus three is four.

4
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.450
Plus five is nine.

5
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.570
Plus seven is sixteen.

6
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.980
Square numbers, every time.

7
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.000
But four cases is not every n.

8
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.520
Is checking lots of cases enough?

9
00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.950
Now picture a line of dominoes
stretching forever, all standing.

10
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.330
Push the first one.

11
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.630
Could that one push settle the
formula for every n at once?

12
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.870
What would you need to
know about the line?

13
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.420
In this mission, you'll write
proofs by mathematical induction,

14
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.020
with their four parts.

15
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.580
You'll use them on sums, on divisibility,

16
00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.240
and on derivatives.

17
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:43.730
Your mission: explain why toppling one
domino proves a formula for every n.
